{
  "schema_version": "pdd.native-cases.v1",
  "story_path": "user_stories/local-contract-layouts.md",
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "I can keep existing Key tables and use exact nested Path ownership with one writer per path and optional schema links."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "I see unrelated JSON skipped once while declared invalid schemas and real copy drift still fail."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "I can read the same local check facts as JSON without changing files or contacting a service."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC4",
      "text": "I keep schema-map validation and copy eligibility while incidental legacy copies cannot hide drift."
    }
  ],
  "boundary": "real CLI argv or runContracts with real safe Git-visible filesystem discovery; no Runtime entry is claimed",
  "setup": {
    "git_repository": true,
    "base_files": {
      "contracts/world.md": "# Shared world\n| Key | What it holds | Writer | Readers | How it is written | Schema |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| items | Values | owner | reader | Replace | contracts/world.md#items |\n\n### items\n```json\n{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":0}}\n```\n",
      "contracts/seed-world.json": "{\"items\":[0,2]}\n"
    },
    "case_files": "Each case starts from base_files, applies delete_files then set_files, all Git-visible. JSON content strings are exact authored bytes. No fixture describes a live app.",
    "observations": "Diagnostics are exact projections on supplied fields; no extra diagnostics, each message nonempty. Counts count canonical schema validations attempted once and present value validations attempted, including invalid verdicts. JSON is exactly one object containing exit_code, checked_records, checked_world_values, skipped_files, diagnostics, warnings; diagnostic messages are nonempty, not fixed prose. Optional source_pointer and target appear only with actual provenance. Preserve all source bytes and modes; count native effects with spies. All cases are active; design revisions are disclosed in the PR body. Warning messages must be finite nonblank strings, not exact prose; missing-schema quantities reflect the number of unique world_keys."
  },
